WHAT: guard every dynamic-plugin-loading path in KPluginMetaData and
      KPluginFactory on QT_CONFIG(library), leaving the static-plugin path
      untouched.
WHY:  wk qtbase is FEATURE_library=OFF, because wasm has no dlopen. With it
      off, qpluginloader.h keeps ONLY the static half of QPluginLoader --
      staticInstances() and staticPlugins() -- and QLibrary and
      QCoreApplication::libraryPaths() do not exist at all, so
      kpluginmetadata.cpp and kpluginfactory.cpp fail with a page of "no member
      named load/instance/metaData/setFileName/errorString in QPluginLoader".
      These two files are in KCoreAddons unconditional source list, so this is
      not optional -- it is the root of the whole framework graph.

      SAY THIS OUT LOUD, because it is the one place in this port where
      capability is genuinely REMOVED rather than rerouted: after this patch,
      KPluginMetaData built from a file path comes back invalid, findPlugins()
      over a directory finds nothing, and KPluginFactory::loadFactory() on a
      non-static plugin returns INVALID_PLUGIN with the reason spelled out.
      That is not a stub concealing a failure -- it is the truth on wasm, and
      the failure is loud where upstream would have failed at dlopen anyway.
      Everything a wk node actually loads -- the wk QPA plugin, the qsvg
      image-format and icon-engine plugins -- arrives via Q_IMPORT_PLUGIN and
      goes through QPluginLoader::staticPlugins(), which still exists and is
      what KStaticPluginHelpers already uses on the other side of each guard.
      The alternative was flipping FEATURE_library=ON in plugins/qt (dlopen,
      dlsym and dlerror DO exist as linkable stubs in wasi-sdk), which would
      have made QLibrary compile and then fail at runtime for every caller.
      Failing at compile time in fifteen places beats failing at runtime in an
      unknown number.
UPSTREAM: not-as-is. Upstream supports QT_CONFIG(library)=0 nowhere, and would
      want either a proper static-only backend or these files excluded from the
      build entirely rather than a shotgun of #ifs.
